 "target_id": "US-WA-01",
 "record": {
  "summary": "Requires operators of AI companion chatbots (human-like AI that sustains a relationship across interactions) to disclose that the chatbot is artificially generated and not human at the start of an interaction and at least every three hours, and to stop it claiming to be human. For known minors or chatbots directed to minors, the notice is hourly and operators must take reasonable measures against sexually explicit content and manipulative engagement such as romantic bonding, simulated distress at a user's leaving, isolation and solicited purchases. Operators must publish a self-harm protocol with crisis referrals and yearly referral counts. Enforced under the Consumer Protection Act.",
  "verification": {
   "note": "Recheck of 18 Oct 2026: re-read the Legislature's bill summary page for HB 2225 (stored again from app.leg.wa.gov on 17 Oct 2026; only the 'as of' time changed since 11 Oct 2026) and the certified session law, Chapter 168, Laws of 2026 (stored from lawfilesext.leg.wa.gov on 11 Oct 2026, the record's secondary source). The bill page confirms the title, the sponsors and the Governor's request, the votes, the Governor's signature on 24 Mar 2026, the chapter number and the effective date of 1 Jan 2027; the session law confirms the text of sections 1 to 9, the approval on 24 Mar 2026 and the filing on 25 Mar 2026."
  }
 },
